    "round4_pc_red_team": {
      "consensus_reject_reason": "No scientific result exists yet; the only defensible mechanism claim depends entirely on the unrun exact-same-pool cloned-state intervention, while CADP and broad failure/branch claims collide with prior work.",
      "scores": {
        "deepseek-v4-pro": {
          "recommendation": "REJECT",
          "score": 2,
          "strongest_reject_reason": "The paper has no executed experiment, and its only defensible novelty is a mechanism-level causal claim that is currently indistinguishable from a definitional identity plus a selective-labeling instance. The decisive cloned-state projection-null experiment is the entire scientific content, and it has not been run. Without it, the paper is a design document with a method (CADP) already reduced by SkillCAT and a representation claim already reduced by TopoCurate."
        },
        "kimi-k3": {
          "recommendation": "REJECT",
          "score": 3,
          "strongest_reject_reason": "The paper proposes a mechanism-level causal claim—that winner-only serving selection censors diagnostic failures from a persistent updater, degrading future skill—but provides zero experimental evidence for this phenomenon. The decisive cloned-state projection-null experiment (F2) has not been run, and the historical R3 runner is explicitly non-executable for the R4 same-pool intervention. Meanwhile, the proposed method (CADP) is a direct collision with SkillCAT (success/failure pairing, first-divergence extraction, contrastive skill editing, replay validation), and the broader claims about failure utility and outcome-filtering discarding branch structure are already established by Rethinking Self-Evolving Agent Skills and TopoCurate. The theoretical contributions are either vacuous (data-processing inequality for a fixed LLM updater), tautological (Gamma-times-delta factorization), or elementary (i.i.d. Bernoulli order statistics). Without the F2 experiment demonstrating that changing the learning projection g(T_K) on identical pools changes future frozen skill, the paper is an unphenomenological design document with method components already published elsewhere."
        }
      },
      "verdict_changing_repair": "Freeze a narrow R4 contract, implement and validate a same-pool runner, then run only the decisive cloned-state projection-null experiment first."
    }
